 <body>
  <center><h2>How to Make Perfect Biryani</h2></center>

<h3>Ingredients</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>500g boneless chicken, cut into bite-sized pieces</li>
    <li>1 medium onion, sliced</li>
    <li>1 medium bell pepper, diced</li>
    <li>1 medium tomato, chopped, plus 1/2 cup tomato puree</li>
    <li>1 tbsp ginger-garlic paste</li>
    <li>2 tbsp oil or ghee</li>
    <li>1 tsp cumin seeds, 1 tsp Kashmiri red chili powder, 1/2 tsp turmeric, 1 tsp coriander powder, 1/2 tsp garam masala</li>
    <li>1 tsp crushed kasuri methi and salt to taste</li>
  </ul>
  
  <h3>Instructions</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Season the chicken with salt, turmeric, and half the red chili powder.</li>
    <li>Sear the chicken in 1 tablespoon of hot oil or ghee for 4 to 5 minutes, then set aside.</li>
    <li>Add remaining oil or ghee, pop cumin seeds, and stir-fry sliced onions and bell peppers for 2 to 3 minutes.</li>
    <li>Add ginger-garlic paste, chopped tomatoes, tomato puree, and remaining spices; cook until thickened.</li>
    <li>Return chicken to the pan, simmer for 4 to 5 minutes, and finish with garam masala and kasuri methi.</li>
  </ol>
  
 </body>
